 "poem": "Ear and Ease, as if the couch were broken,\nSat cowering near their partner's shoulder;\nAnd there in agitation and provoke\nThe cry of Thalia; for she arose,\nUrge to man, and urged him with delight.\nHer eyes, so red from thirst, his face admiration\nFelt; a feverish frenzy arrived.\nHe dropped each flower he had reputation,\nNow was her temper very kind again;\nShe sat on his arm, and tenderly kissed\nHis hand in very affectionate disdain:\nBut whereat I gazed, and found quickly",
